","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Tteokbokki, topokki or simmered rice cake, is a Korean food made from small-sized garae-tteok (long, white, cylinder-shaped rice cakes) called tteokmyeon (떡면; lit. 'rice cake noodles') or commonly tteokbokki-tteok (떡볶이 떡; lit. 'tteokbokki rice cakes'). It is often paired with eomuk (fish cakes), boiled eggs, and scallions, and seasoned with spicy gochujang (chili paste). Less often, it is served in a non-spicy ganjang-based (soy) sauce, which is sometimes called gungjung-tteokbokki (royal court tteokbokki)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-tteokbokki"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tteokbokki"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Korean cuisine","cuisine/korean-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Fishcake","ingredient/fishcake"],["Gochujang","ingredient/gochujang"],["Tteok","ingredient/tteok"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Maangchi","ref":"site/maangchi-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"maangchi.com","note":"Maangchi's Korean recipe site and YouTube channel, one of the best known English sources for Korean cooking.","url":"https://www.maangchi.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Korean Bapsang","ref":"site/koreanbapsang-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"koreanbapsang.com","note":"Home-style Korean recipes from Hyosun, a Korean-American mom.","url":"https://www.koreanbapsang.com/category/recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Korean cuisine","links":[["Bap (rice dish)","dish/bap-rice-dish"],["Bibim-guksu","dish/bibim-guksu"],["Bibimbap","dish/bibimbap"],["Bosintang","dish/bosintang"],["Cheonggukjang","dish/cheonggukjang"],["Doenjang","dish/doenjang"],["Garak-guksu","dish/garak-guksu"],["Gochujang","dish/gochujang"],["Gopchang","dish/gopchang"],["Hwajeon","dish/hwajeon"],["Jijimi","dish/jijimi"],["Jokbal","dish/jokbal"],["Korean restaurant","dish/korean-restaurant"],["Maekjeok","dish/maekjeok"],["Maeun-tang","dish/maeun-tang"],["Makchang","dish/makchang"],["Mandu-guk","dish/mandu-guk"],["Mandu-gwa","dish/mandu-gwa"],["Meat jun","dish/meat-jun"],["Meju","dish/meju"],["Morkovcha","dish/morkovcha"],["Scorched rice","dish/scorched-rice"],["Seon (food)","dish/seon-food"],["Sungnyung","dish/sungnyung"],["Wakame","dish/wakame"],["Yakgwa","dish/yakgwa"],["Yukpo","dish/yukpo"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/56/Korean.snacks-Tteokbokki-08.jpg/500px-Korean.snacks-Tteokbokki-08.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"by jetalone (flickr)","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Korean.snacks-Tteokbokki-08.jpg"}},"cookbook/my-life-my-food-my-kurdistan":{"t":"book","r":"cookbook/my-life-my-food-my-kurdistan","n":"My Life, My Food, My Kurdistan","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Cookbooks","cookbooks"]],"sub":"Cookbook by Chiman Zebari","square":true,"suggested":true,"intro":[["Family recipes and memoir from Iraqi Kurdistan."]],"actions":[],"sections":[{"h":"Cuisines it covers","count":1,"links":[["Kurdish cuisine","cuisine/kurdish-cuisine"]]}]}}